"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[24643],{124643:e=>{e.exports='# Find a Detection Rule\n\nHow to find or retrieve a **detection rule** by ID or by name. Use when the user asks to view, get, or modify a specific rule.\n\nFor rule counts, call **apiFindLakewatchDetectionRules**. Omit `query` for the total number of rules, or pass the relevant phrase for filtered counts such as “CrowdStrike rules”. Use `totalMatches` in the response; do not list every rule name just to count them.\n\n## User provides a rule ID\n\nRule IDs are random-generated and **start with `rl-`** (e.g. `rl-xyz789abc`). When the user gives an ID explicitly or one that starts with `rl-`, call `apiGetLakewatchResourceById` with `resourceType: "rule"` and `resourceId` set to that ID.\n\n```json\n{\n  "thoughts": "User provided rule ID \'rl-xyz789abc\'. Retrieving the detection rule directly.",\n  "resourceType": "rule",\n  "resourceId": "rl-xyz789abc"\n}\n```\n\n## User provides a rule name\n\nWhen the user references a rule by human-readable name (e.g. “brute force login detection”):\n\n1. Call **apiFindLakewatchDetectionRules** with the name or relevant text. It checks cached rule-list pages first, then scans paginated API results without returning every rule to the conversation.\n2. If the response has matching results, extract the ID (from `metadata.name`/`id`).\n3. Call **apiGetLakewatchResourceById** with `resourceType: "rule"` and that `resourceId`.\n\n**Multiple matches**: Present all with ID, display name, and description; ask the user which one they want.\n\n**No match**: Tell the user no detection rule matched; suggest listing all rules or creating a new one.\n'}}]);
